{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--sakhalin-elder-ani-conjunctive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin elder speech, the conjunctive particle 'ani expresses means, method, circumstance, or reason ('by', 'while', 'because').","ja":"樺太方言の老人層の言葉において、接続助詞 'ani は手段・方法・付帯状況・理由（「〜によって、〜して、〜ながら、〜ので」）を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["elder speech"]},"forms":["'ani"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0039-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0103-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--shizunai-koraci-verbal-nominalizer","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"In the Shizunai dialect, the comparative particle koraci can follow verbs as a nominalizer, presenting the nominalized predicate as a standard of comparison for the main predicate.","ja":"静内方言において、比較助詞 koraci は動詞に後続して名詞化辞として機能し、名詞化された述語を主述語の比較の基準として提示する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["following verbs"]},"forms":["koraci"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0256-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0257-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--shizunai-koraci-stative-befitting","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"In the Shizunai dialect, when koraci follows stative verbs, it conveys the meaning of befitting the state denoted by that verb.","ja":"静内方言において、koraci が状態動詞に後続する場合、その動詞が表す状態に「ふさわしい」という意味を表すことがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["following stative verbs"]},"forms":["koraci"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0258-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--shizunai-koraci-verbal-nominalizer","differs_in":"scope","note":"Specializes the function of post-verbal koraci specifically to stative verbs where it denotes befitting that state."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--the-conjunction-kane-expresses-while-simultaneous-action","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunction kane expresses 'while' (simultaneous action).","ja":"kane は「ながら」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0160-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--neeno-is-used-in-the-sense-of-so","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses"],"statement":{"en":"neeno is used in the sense of 'so as to...' or 'like...'.","ja":"neeno は「～するように」の意味を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["neeno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0077-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--pahno-expresses-extent-or-temporal-limit-to-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"pahno expresses extent or temporal limit ('to the extent that', 'until').","ja":"pahno は限度や限時（「～する程」「～するまで」）を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pahno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0077-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--the-particle-kane-means-to-the-extent-of","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"The particle 'kane' means 'to the extent of' or 'to the degree that'.","ja":"kane は「〜ほどに, 〜くらいに」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0071-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--conjunctive-kane-expresses-being-to-the-same-degree","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"Conjunctive 'kane' expresses being to the same degree as something, and is often used especially when describing a situation metaphorically and hyperbolically beyond reality.","ja":"接続助詞的な kane は、あるものと同程度であることを表す形式であるが、特に事態を現実以上にオーバーに比喩的に表現する場合によく用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--koraci-means-like-just-as-or-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"'koraci' means 'like', 'just as', or 'as'.","ja":"koraci は「〜のように，〜の通りに，〜のままに」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["koraci"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--pak-means-to-the-extent-of-or-up","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"'pak' means 'to the extent of' or 'up to about'.","ja":"pak は「〜ほど, 〜くらいまで」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pak"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0073-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--the-particle-kane-expresses-an-exaggerated-degree","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"The particle kane expresses an exaggerated degree.","ja":"kane は「オーバーな程度」を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0364-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--kane-functions-as-a-particle-meaning-to-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--degree-pakno"],"statement":{"en":"kane functions as a particle meaning 'to the extent of, such as, in the manner of'.","ja":"kane は「ほど，など，ように」を意味する副助詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0386-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--in-saru-and-chitose-kane-functions-across-conjunctive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--no-particle"],"statement":{"en":"In Saru and Chitose, kane functions across conjunctive particles, auxiliary verbs, and secondary auxiliaries, expressing marked circumstances such as in stock phrases pas kane terke kane 'running and jumping' or ikayop takup se kane an 'bearing only a quiver'.","ja":"沙流方言や千歳方言においては kane は接続助詞、助動詞、副助動詞にまたがる性質を持ち、pas kane terke kane や ikayop takup se kane an のように何か特筆すべき状況を表す場合に用いられ、kor や wa とは異なる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0339-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--in-the-shizunai-dialect-the-contemporal-conjunctionalizer-kane","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--no-particle"],"statement":{"en":"In the Shizunai dialect, the contemporal conjunctionalizer kane indicates that two acts or events occur simultaneously.","ja":"静内方言において、同時接続詞 kane は2つの行為または事象が同時に生じることを表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0244-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--after-stative-verbs-kane-indicates-the-circumstances-or","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--no-particle"],"statement":{"en":"After stative verbs, kane indicates the circumstances or state that form the background of the following sentence.","ja":"状態動詞の後頭で kane は後続文の背景となる状況または状態を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["after stative verbs"]},"forms":["kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0244-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--in-affirmative-sentences-the-conjunction-particle-no-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--no-particle"],"statement":{"en":"In affirmative sentences, the conjunction particle no is used in adverbial clauses expressing a stative event or an incidental circumstance.","ja":"肯定文において接続助詞 no は、状態的事象や付帯状況を示す副詞節で用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["in affirmative sentences"]},"forms":["no"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:takahashi2022@handbook-epub/l0120-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--the-form-sem-korachi-is-semantically-equivalent-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"The form sem-korachi is semantically equivalent to korachi 'like, as'.","ja":"sem-korachi は korachi（〜の如く）と同義である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["sem-korachi","korachi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0176-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--the-conjunction-expressing-as-if-appears-as-pekor","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunction expressing 'as if' appears as pekor in Saru and Chitose, pokor in Horobetsu, and pokon in Shizunai, Tokachi, Bihoro, Shiranuka, Kushiro, and Ishikari.","ja":"「〜するかのように」を表す接続助詞は、沙流・千歳方言で pekor、幌別方言で pokor、静内、十勝、美幌、白糠、釧路、石狩で pokon となる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kitami","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kushiro","doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pekor","pokor","pokon"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0351-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--apekor-is-mainly-used-in-saru-and-chitose","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"apekor is mainly used in Saru and Chitose; no examples have been found for apokor, but apokon is recorded in Tokachi and Yakumo.","ja":"apekor は沙流・千歳方言で主に使われる形で、apokor は例が見当たらないが、apokon は十勝と八雲に記録がある。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/yakumo"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["apekor","apokon","apokor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0351-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--apekor-often-occurs-in-the-construction-apekor-an","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"apekor often occurs in the construction apekor an ('just like / as if'), a usage that pekor appears not to have.","ja":"apekor an で「まるで〜したような」という表現をとることが多いが、これは pekor には無い用法のようである。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["apekor an","apekor","pekor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0351-03","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--apekor-like-pekor-compares-the-following-clause-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"apekor, like pekor, compares the following clause to the preceding clause, but the preceding clause often expresses a situation that is utterly impossible.","ja":"apekor は pekor と同じように後文を前文でたとえる場合に使うが、前文がとうていありえないような事態を表している場合が多い。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["apekor","pekor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0351-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--kotom-no-as-if-apparently-seemingly-expresses-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"kotom(no) ('as if / apparently / seemingly') expresses a conjecture about something that is actually happening or likely to happen.","ja":"kotom(no)「〜する（した）ように」「〜する（した）らしく」は、実際に起こっていること、起こりそうなことを推測する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kotom","kotomno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0351-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--noyne-as-if-apparently-seemingly-expresses-a-conjecture","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"noyne ('as if / apparently / seemingly') expresses a conjecture about something that is actually happening or likely to happen.","ja":"noyne「〜する(した)ように」「〜する(した)らしく」は、実際に起こっていること、起こりそうなことを推測する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["noyne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0352-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--noyne-is-geographically-narrower-than-kotom-being-restricted","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"noyne is geographically narrower than kotom, being restricted almost entirely to Saru, Chitose, Horobetsu, and Shizunai dialects.","ja":"方言差としては noyne はほぼ沙流・千歳・幌別・静内方言に限られていて、kotom より地域的に狭い範囲で用いられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["noyne","kotom"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0352-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--noyne-is-frequently-used-in-constructions-such-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"noyne is frequently used in constructions such as noyne ramu ('think that...'), noyne yaynu ('think that...'), noyne humas ('have an atmosphere of...'), and noyne siran ('appear to...').","ja":"noyne は、noyne ramu「〜のように思う」、noyne yaynu「〜のように思う」、noyne humas「〜のような雰囲気だ」、noyne siran「〜のような様子だ」というような構文で使われることが多い。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["noyne ramu","noyne yaynu","noyne humas","noyne siran"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0352-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--kotom-no-means-like-or-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"'kotom(no)' means 'like' or 'as'.","ja":"kotom(no) は「〜ように」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kotom","kotomno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--kotom-no-is-used-mainly-in-poetic-elevated","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"'kotom(no)' is used mainly in poetic/elevated language, and is frequently followed by 'a-esanniyo' ('to think').","ja":"kotom(no) は主に雅語で用いられ、後ろに a-esanniyo「思う」が来ることが多い。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kotom","kotomno","a-esanniyo"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--n-no-means-like-just-as-or-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"'néno' means 'like', 'just as', or 'as'.","ja":"néno は「〜のように，〜の通りに，〜のままに」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["néno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--noyne-expresses-inference-based-on-external-appearance-or","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"'noyne' expresses inference based on external appearance or other evidence, meaning 'seemingly' or 'as if'.","ja":"noyne は外見その他の証拠からの推量を表し、「〜ように」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["noyne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0072-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--p-kor-expresses-contrary-to-fact-comparison-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"'pékor' expresses contrary-to-fact comparison, meaning 'as if' or 'as though'.","ja":"pékor は事実に反する比況を表し、「〜かのように」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pékor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0073-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--while-combinations-like-a-p-kor-can-be","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topics":["topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses","topic:complex/manner-and-degree-adverbial-clauses--simile-inference"],"statement":{"en":"While combinations like 'a pékor' can be interpreted as the anterior particle 'a' plus 'pékor' ('as if having done'), there are tokens where the accent falls on 'a', suggesting the possibility of recognizing a distinct form 'ápekor'.","ja":"a pékor は「た・かのように」と解釈されるが、アクセントが a に置かれる例があり、ápekor という pékor とは別の形式を認める必要がある可能性もある。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["a","pékor","ápekor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0074-01","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
